<h1>What is Programming?</h1>
<p><strong>Programming</strong> is the process of giving instructions to a computer to perform specific tasks. These instructions are written in a language that computers can understand, known as a <strong>programming language</strong>.</p>

<div class="highlight">
    <p>In simple terms: Programming is how we tell computers what to do.</p>
</div>

<h2>Examples of what we can build with programming:</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Websites (e.g., Facebook, Instagram)</li>
    <li>Mobile apps (e.g., WhatsApp, TikTok)</li>
    <li>Games (e.g., Fortnite, FIFA)</li>
    <li>Software tools (e.g., Microsoft Word, Excel)</li>
    <li>AI systems (e.g., ChatGPT, voice assistants)</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🧠</span>Why is Programming Important?</h2>
<ul>
    <li>It automates tasks and increases efficiency.</li>
    <li>It powers nearly all modern technology.</li>
    <li>It helps solve complex problems.</li>
    <li>It's a valuable skill for careers in tech and beyond.</li>
</ul>

<h2><span class="emoji">🧪</span>Types of Programming Languages</h2>
<p>There are many programming languages, each with its own use case. Here are some examples:</p>

